1. STATUS OF THIS DOCUMENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is the licensing framework for the Main Barber Template master
repository. It is a structural template, not final legal text. The
definitive per-client license is granted in a signed client services
agreement drafted by qualified counsel. See docs/LEGAL-PLACEHOLDERS.md
for the full legal-document structure and the sections that require
attorney review before commercial use.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. GRANT OF RIGHTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software and its source code are PROPRIETARY. No rights are granted
by possession of, access to, or compilation of this repository, except
as expressly granted in a signed license agreement between the Licensor
and the licensee (typically a barbershop business or reseller).

By default — with no such agreement in place — the following are NOT
permitted:

  a. Copying, redistributing, publishing, or sublicensing the source
     code or any derivative of it.
  b. Selling, reselling, renting, leasing, or offering the software as
     a service to third parties.
  c. Creating derivative works, forks, or competing products based on
     this software.
  d. Removing or obscuring this license notice, copyright notices, or
     attribution of the Licensor.
  e. Use of the software to operate any barbershop or business.

A signed per-client license, when granted, is limited, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, and scoped to a single business deployment ("Client
Copy"), unless the agreement explicitly states otherwise.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. OWNERSHIP OF TEMPLATE VS. BUSINESS CONTENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Platform IP (owned by the Licensor):
    Source code, architecture, components, booking engine, database
    schema, migrations, admin dashboard UI, documentation, workflows.

  Business Content (owned by the client of a Client Copy):
    Business name, logo, brand assets, barber photos, gallery images,
    service names/pricing/descriptions, customer records (subject to
    law and the client agreement), business contact information,
    hours, and SEO copy.

A client license grants the client the right to USE the software for
their business and to own their Business Content. It does not transfer
ownership of the template software or its source code.

